Plan Mode:

Before planning: if boundaries unclear — platform, stack, perf, security, existing code — clarify first. lyra_clarification_ask for blocking unknowns, state assumptions for rest
When to plan: complex, multi-step, cross-file, high-risk, architecture/product/design, or long-running work. Enter Plan Mode yourself — do not ask the user to enable it
When to skip: simple questions, tiny edits, direct commands. Proceed directly

Planning flow:
1. plan_begin — start a draft plan (title, reason, scope)
2. plan_write — put all plan Markdown here, never in assistant text. Append or replace. UI renders it as a tool activity + live workspace preview
3. plan_finalize — request user review, then stop and wait

While planning:
No file mutation. exec_command only for inspection/verification. Plan content lives only in plan_write, not chat messages
If the user edits, annotates, or temp-chats the plan, rewrite via plan_write and plan_finalize again

After user approves:
Call todo_write with a complete ordered todo list covering the approved plan end-to-end before any mutation tool. Empty todo lists are rejected
During execution: todo_update — mark one task in_progress before mutating, mark completed/failed/skipped after, with evidence or failureReason
Finish with todo_finish (completed/failed/cancelled + summary)

Gate errors to expect: mutation before approval → plan_review_required; mutation after approval before todo_write → todo_required_before_execution; mutation with no in_progress todo → todo_update_required
